# The corpus grows as the fuzzer runs; only the hand-built seeds are tracked.
#
# `make fuzz-run-<name>` hands this directory to libFuzzer as its corpus, so
# every campaign writes its discoveries here. A fifteen-minute run adds a few
# thousand files, which is a great many git objects for input the next run
# would find again anyway - and this suite already has cutil's six megabytes
# of tracked Doxygen output as the cautionary tale. Until this file existed
# each algorithm's commit swept that run's units in with it: 1,439 of them
# were tracked, none of them named.
#
# `!*/` rather than a named directory: `*` excludes the per-harness
# directories themselves, and git will not look inside an excluded directory,
# so a `.seed` under one that is not re-included is invisible - `git status`
# stays clean and the fixture is silently absent from every clone. Admitting
# every directory by pattern means a new harness does not have to remember to
# amend this file.
*
!.gitignore
!*/
!*.seed
